		<defName>CGF1_MWP_Type69_</defName>
		<label>Type 69</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x39mm. 20-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.
		
The Type 69 is a Chinese reverse engineering of the M16 based off of captured rifles from the Vietnam War. Though the design of the receiver is quite close to that of the M16, significant deviations were made in producing the weapon's furniture (made out of wood rather than polymer on the Type 69), and most importantly, the weapon was altered to fire the 7.62x39mm out of unusual curved 20-round magazines. The weapon never seems to have been used in combat or exported, as it was likely intended as a prototype.</description>
